Subject: [PATCH 03498/11362] [outer-loop] Program-generalization first swing:
 imagination-planning deepens L1, walls on hidden state

Reused the existing E3 executable-world-model framework (induce -> WorldModelVerifier ->
plan_in_model BFS-in-imagination) to test the leaderboard-leader deepening lever
(arXiv:2605.05138) on our stack. Harness scripts/experiments/experiment_program_gen.py
(per-game artifacts, all 3 adversarial-verify clean).

- LEVER WORKS at L1: hand-induced a faithful tu93 4-dir maze-nav world model
  (results/arc_e3/tu93/world_model_nav.py; 100% movement accuracy, 99/99 moves, 0
  false-blocks). plan_in_model planned an 18-action L1 path entirely in imagination,
  executed it, leveled up, fresh-env reproduced.
- Deepening to L2 is HIDDEN-STATE bound: L2 plan matched reality 3-4 steps then env
  game-over at a run-dependent step (tu93 non-idempotent-reset parity, registry gotcha
  #7). Same hidden-state wall the value approach hit; tu93 in wa30/ls20 family.
- Existing E3 models do not generalize: ka59 (cell-recall 0.43, too noisy for BFS) and
  sc25 (PATCH_BY_KEY memorized, 0.06 off-table) reach only L0 in imagination.

Forward (.425+, folded into known-issues + research note): the energy/config state for
the wa30/ls20/tu93 family must carry the hidden parity/budget LATENT dimension;
fresh-env-per-candidate branch search is the registry's deepening fix; aim the local-GGUF
proposer at induction fidelity.

